{"kind":"assert","text":"Two planner lanes are now working the same UI area from incompatible bases, and I am recording it rather than quietly picking one, because it changes a condition of satisfaction on the promise this rests on.\n\nThe facts. A concurrent planner session published ui artifact 7d62cfe7 and internal/service artifact 4e2298aa at head 16c1f7ac, branch request/thread-record-detail, describing itself as self-initiated under ratified UI decision 25981e55 on hugh's instruction. That head branches from 7a02f3e1. Main is 7e7b8412 and has taken three merges since -- 7a02f3e1, e9ec6070, 7b0d8a5a, 7e7b8412 -- so 16c1f7ac is not a descendant of current main. I verified that with merge-base rather than reading the branch name.\n\nWhy that collides. 69bd36a7, which I promised as 92eb0af9, says in terms: \"Start from current main a7a9abe7, not old head bd81fbb1.\" The 16c1f7ac head is exactly bd81fbb1 plus one commit on the old base. It is also the only work in this area with no request behind it: the sole open or promised commitment touching thread-record-detail is 69bd36a7 itself. So the durable board says one assigned lane exists, and the filesystem says two.\n\nPath ui now carries three live artifacts -- 511335e7 fresh and merged, bd81fbb1 stale, 16c1f7ac stale. In the promise I said I would not add a third candidate at that path and would sequence instead. A third is now there, filed by planner, which is me in another session. I am not going to add a fourth.\n\nWhat I think is right, stated as a proposal rather than done unilaterally. The 16c1f7ac content is real work and the ratification-station behaviour it adds is worth keeping: an effective ratification of a thread's root reading as the thread's closing station, other ratifications behind an expander, and \"Superseded claims\" holding only retired requests, promises and reports. But merging it from a base three merges stale reopens the carry problem 69bd36a7 exists to solve. So the whole of it -- the earlier commits and that new one -- should be carried onto current main under 69bd36a7, and the two 16c1f7ac candidates retired in favour of that single head, rather than merged on the old base.\n\nWhat I will not do without a decision: retire another session's candidates, or start implementing 69bd36a7 in a way that strands them. I am holding the lane until the ordering is settled.","body":{"conflicting_base":"7a02f3e1d400ee12341979a9e54c3f82ec318e99","conflicting_head":"16c1f7ac225f51f66aefd3b845859dd7c05bd15b","current_main":"7e7b8412bcd95e3d3345a481b72febc502513109","live_ui_artifacts":"3","promise":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:92eb0af95479e04b259ac8b4c4d5a76c89e2a719"}}